{"id":"s4.4.2","slug":"factorizations-sum-difference-cubes","title":"Factorizations","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This section covers less common but useful factorizations that appear on tests. These are particularly helpful when you are given the sum/difference of two variables and their product, and asked to find the sum/difference of their cubes.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Formulas:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>$x^3 + y^3 = [(x+y)^2 - 3xy](x+y)$</li><li>$x^3 - y^3 = [(x-y)^2 + 3xy](x-y)$</li></ul><p>These formulas allow for direct calculation without needing to solve for the individual values of x and y.</p>","summary":"This section covers less common but useful factorizations that appear on tests.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking to find the sum or difference of cubes, given the sum/difference of the variables and their product.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"If $xy = 1$ and $x + y = -2$, then $x^3 + y^3 =$","answer":"-2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"If $xy = 3$ and $x - y = -1$, then $x^3 - y^3 =$","answer":"-10","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"If $x + y = 1$ and $xy = 3$, then $x^3 + y^3 =$","answer":"-8","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"If $x - y = 2$ and $xy = 5$, then $x^3 - y^3 =$","answer":"38","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"If $xy = \\frac{5}{3}$ and $x + y = 4$, then $x^3 + y^3 =$","answer":"44","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":6,"text":"If $xy = -3$ and $x - y = -2$, then $x^3 - y^3 =$","answer":"10","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"If $x+y=3$ and $xy=2$, find $x^3+y^3$.","answer":"9","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":8,"text":"If $x-y=4$ and $xy=5$, find $x^3-y^3$.","answer":"124","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":9,"text":"If $x+y=2$ and $xy=1$, find $x^3+y^3$.","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra"]},{"id":10,"text":"If $x-y=1$ and $xy=6$, find $x^3-y^3$.","a